>It sounds like your answer is yes; since the rustproofed item
>may be selected to be simonized again.  My original question
>was that since the selection process is random does it only
>select from the nonrust- or fireproofed choices.  You seem to
>be saying that you need to remove any previously proofed armor
>to ensure that a nonproofed piece of armor is used this time.

hopefully this will clear the issue once and for all (or at least
permanently confuse EVERYONE)...

YES, the scroll can work on *any* piece of armor you are wearing,
regardless of whether or not it has already been proofed.  So, if you
want to GUARANTEE that a certain piece of armor gets affected, make
sure it's the ONLY piece of armor that you are wearing.

And as I said before, if the scroll does decide to proof something
that's already been proofed, nothing bad happens - it's not a toggle.
The armor stays proofed, and you just wasted the scroll.

